          "item": {
            "@type": "NewsArticle",
            "headline": "OpenAI's TanStack npm Supply Chain Attack Compromised Two Employee Devices",
            "articleSection": "Policy & Rights",
            "abstract": "OpenAI has confirmed that two employee devices were compromised after malware hidden in poisoned npm packages associated with the TanStack JavaScript ecosystem reached company machines, resulting in the theft of a limited amount of internal credential material. The incident is the latest in a string of software supply chain attacks targeting AI companies and highlights how attackers are using trusted open-source ecosystems as entry points into high-value AI organisations. OpenAI says it has contained the breach and is working with the npm security team.",
            "url": "https://www.theregister.com/security/2026/05/15/openai-caught-in-tanstack-npm-supply-chain-chaos-after-employee-devices-compromised/5241019",
            "publisher": {
              "@type": "NewsMediaOrganization",
              "name": "The AI Chronicle",
